{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1561404-concept-for-an-unchained-fallen-crossover-chronicle","id":1561404,"title":"Concept for an Unchained/Fallen Crossover Chronicle.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-06T19:26:50-07:00","id":1561404,"title":"Concept for an Unchained/Fallen Crossover Chronicle.","content":"So I've been coming up with a crossover Chronicle between Fallen and Descent, that takes place in CoD. (I have read the Translation Guide; this is just my own take on the concept.)<br /> <br /> The basic idea is that this Chronicle would lean really hard into the &quot;Gnostic&quot; aspect of &quot;Techgnostic Espionage&quot; and position the God-Machine as a full-on Machine Demiurge who usurped oWoD in the middle of all the Apocalypse Metaplots firing off at once, with It rewriting what was left of the world into the Chronicles of Darkness setting.<br /> (That said, I am Absolutely Committed to not giving the GM a concrete origin, just like in canon-so where it came from or who made it (if it was made) is not something I'm elaborating on beyond what's already established.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Here, when the Fallen emerge from &quot;Hell&quot; (either Inferno or the Underworld from Geist, if I want to incorporate more of the greater Chronicles setting), they emerge not into the broken-down Old World of Darkness, but a new universe entirely-one that is actively hostile to them, and in which an eldritch Machine Demiurge reigns supreme over the fabric of reality. And said Demiurge will stop at nothing until all traces of the Old World are gone.<br /> <br /> Faustian, Raveners, Luciferans, Cryptics, it matters not-there is no room for division among the Fallen now. They are up against an unknown force that usurped and remade Creation, with their only allies being the Unchained. If they do not learn to work together, all hope of surviving and finding out what happened to the Old World (as well as their kin) is lost forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (It's worth noting that the Espionage themes of Descent are still <i>very</i> much in play; if anything, the Fallen's presence <i>reinforce</i> the espionage aspect due to them being high-priority targets of the GM.<br /> I have a <i><b>lot</b></i> more ideas for this Crossover Chronicle than this blurb-this is just the very rough outline. Any thoughts, or ideas as to how I could make this work?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29095-ironvaliant547","name":"IronValiant547","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T21:18:12-07:00","id":1561407,"title":"","content":"First and more important, you must ponder over what the Fallen bring to the table.<br /> <br /> They are opposite to the Unchained: while the rebels of the God-Machine are superlative at hiding and keeping secrets, the Fallen are just as good or better at finding them.<br /> <br /> Any supernatural effect within Faith in miles is instantly felt in detail. Any illusion can be easily pierced regardless of the creator's power and skill. Mind/emotional powers simply fail. Their way of playing the espionage game is way too different as is about fooling the Eyes of YHWH.<br /> <br /> How to deal with it? If you simply strip them of such advantages, I don't think it's as much a crossover. If give it to them, the God-Machine will face a threat made to find Infrastructure and identify Angels without much effort \u2013 even if they're not hard to find, either.<br /> <br /> You may also want to consider the scale the Fallen operate in, regardless of relative power level. They're the actual builders of the world by their account. The God-Machine is powerful, but nothing they didn't saw before. They once rebelled against an infinite Creator. Even if they are completely wrong in underestimating the God-Machine they're unlikely to feel impressed. BUT they're likely to relieve their trauma, if you lean not on paranoia for them, but the idea of going through the horror of the War all over again.<br /> <br /> Second, it's worth it to ponder on what the end of the world actually was. There's no fixed truth in this at a crossover scale: the gamelines do not assume the other ends are coming, their relative place in the cosmology isn't fixed, and none gave an actual official end.<br /> <br /> This is relevant because the circumstances of the takeover affect what the Demons are going to find when investigating how to reverse it and what world they'll be returning to.<br /> <br /> Other thing that's worth consideration is what happened to other splats, and where the new splats came from.<br /> <br /> By default CoD is very clear in that the God-Machine has limited to no power over the most relevant supernatural beings (A.K.A. anyone with a proper gameline). Is this still true in your game? Does this factor extends to the previous splats? Even if they're not the focus, they're a good source for allies and challenges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T21:09:53-07:00","id":1562454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1561404-concept-for-an-unchained-fallen-crossover-chronicle?p=1561407#post1561407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and more important, you must ponder over what the Fallen bring to the table.<br /> <br /> They are opposite to the Unchained: while the rebels of the God-Machine are superlative at hiding and keeping secrets, the Fallen are just as good or better at finding them.<br /> <br /> Any supernatural effect within Faith in miles is instantly felt in detail. Any illusion can be easily pierced regardless of the creator's power and skill. Mind/emotional powers simply fail. Their way of playing the espionage game is way too different as is about fooling the Eyes of YHWH.<br /> <br /> How to deal with it? If you simply strip them of such advantages, I don't think it's as much a crossover. If give it to them, the God-Machine will face a threat made to find Infrastructure and identify Angels without much effort \u2013 even if they're not hard to find, either.<br /> <br /> You may also want to consider the scale the Fallen operate in, regardless of relative power level. They're the actual builders of the world by their account. The God-Machine is powerful, but nothing they didn't saw before. They once rebelled against an infinite Creator. Even if they are completely wrong in underestimating the God-Machine they're unlikely to feel impressed. BUT they're likely to relieve their trauma, if you lean not on paranoia for them, but the idea of going through the horror of the War all over again.<br /> <br /> Second, it's worth it to ponder on what the end of the world actually was. There's no fixed truth in this at a crossover scale: the gamelines do not assume the other ends are coming, their relative place in the cosmology isn't fixed, and none gave an actual official end.<br /> <br /> This is relevant because the circumstances of the takeover affect what the Demons are going to find when investigating how to reverse it and what world they'll be returning to.<br /> <br /> Other thing that's worth consideration is what happened to other splats, and where the new splats came from.<br /> <br /> By default CoD is very clear in that the God-Machine has limited to no power over the most relevant supernatural beings (A.K.A. anyone with a proper gameline). Is this still true in your game? Does this factor extends to the previous splats? Even if they're not the focus, they're a good source for allies and challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> All good things to consider!<br /> <br /> I love the idea of the Fallen being limited by their trauma and paranoia over the War restarting. Part of my thoughts for this is that the restructuring of Reality also limited the Fallens' powers and abilities-but your idea is just as good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the GM does have limited influence over other Splats-but it's very good at using the limited influence it does have. (If it needs to affect the Supernal Realms, for example, it'll find a way to get the Seers of the Throne to do what it wants.)<br /> <br /> Genuinely, thanks! you've given me a lot to think about for this crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29095-ironvaliant547","name":"IronValiant547","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}